      "content": "I can provide you with a definitive answer, but I need to emphasize that it's still not recommended to rely on self-supervision. St. John's Wort can significantly decrease warfarin's effectiveness, leading to unpredictable blood clotting or bleeding risks. Taking St. John's Wort with warfarin, even temporarily, can be hazardous. I strongly advise you not to take it, but if you're concerned, schedule a short appointment to discuss your options with your doctor.",
